This problem can't be solved completely due to the complexity of csharp code (which has more than what you have shown from your code). Also, there are no such comments in the given code. But here is how you might code such a task:

```python
import re

def parse_comments(text):
    assert_comments = []
    lines = text.split("\n")
    for line in lines:
        match = re.search(r'// @@@ (.*)', line)
        if match:
            comment = match.group(1)
            assert_comments.append(comment)
    return assert_comments

# Test the function
text = """
public class TestClass
{
    public int Property { get; set; }

    // @@@ This is an example of an assert statement
    public void TestMethod()
    {
        // Sample function body
    }
}
"""

assert_comments = parse_comments(text)
for comment in assert_comments:
    print("Debug.Assert(" + comment + ");")
```

In this python script, we're using regex(`re` module) to find all lines that have comments that start with "@@@", and then we simply print them out in Debug.Assert format. This won't handle all types or levels of csharp syntax, but should work for many basic csharp use cases.--------------------